  "notes": "The 1999 flag-tail scheme (standard-1999) with the SkyCargo titles; no 'www.emirates.com' on the freighters. The title layout matches the 2023-scheme freighters (cargo), measured on A6-EWK; checked against A6-EFM (2025) and A6-EFO (2024). Worn in 2023-2026 photos by A6-EFL, EFM, EFO, EFS, EFT, EFU, being repainted in the 2023 scheme. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on A6-EWK (777F): 'Emirates' (x 0.100 to 0.309), 'SkyCargo' (0.102 to 0.177) and the red sweep (leaving the crown about x 0.82 to 0.85, its point about x 0.70, y -0.54) agree with the drawing within the photo's perspective; the Arabic title's aft end is behind the wing, so its length (0.077) is the 2023 scheme's 4.9 m on the A350 taken onto the 777F (low). The red sweep is smooth.",
  "history": "Emirates SkyCargo's 777Fs (from 2008) were delivered in this scheme with the SkyCargo titles; replaced from 2024-2025 by the 2023 livery (cargo). The earlier 747-400Fs (Atlas Air, to 2013) wore it too."
